cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Veritas Mesh in your research, an audit, or a deployment, please cite it as below."
title: "Veritas Mesh: An Open Protocol for Verifiable Institutional Compliance"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Pleşca"
    given-names: "Ciprian Ştefan"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
    country: RO
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ciprian-LocalPulse/veritas-mesh"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - zero-knowledge proofs
  - verifiable computation
  - regulatory compliance
  - privacy-preserving audit
  - institutional trust
  - open-source research
abstract: >
  Veritas Mesh is an open protocol and reference implementation for
  cryptographically verifiable institutional attestations. It allows
  regulated institutions — financial, healthcare, and governmental —
  to prove that a policy or invariant was satisfied for a given action
  without disclosing the private data underlying that action. The
  project is developed as independent, public-interest research for
  the benefit of humanity, with no institutional affiliation.
